---
id: weegloo-minimal-load
type: rule
title: Weegloo - fetch the minimum, compute on the client
description: >
  Foundational cost rule for every Weegloo integration. Each request fetches only the data the
  current step actually needs (select, server-side filters, limit, totalCount, image style presets,
  CDA for public reads), and every computation that does NOT require server-side authority runs on
  the CLIENT (browser for web, the app for mobile/native) from data already fetched - never as an
  extra Weegloo round-trip or a Script run. Also fixes the counterweight (secrets, authorization,
  atomicity, concurrency, unbounded queries stay server-side) and the forbidden load anti-patterns
  (polling loops, paging to count, N+1 by-id reads, fetch-all-then-filter, unprojected reads).
---

rules:
  - section: The principle (non-negotiable — applies to every Weegloo integration)
    items:
      - "**Weegloo is shared, metered infrastructure — every call is something you SPEND, not something that is free.** Two obligations follow, and they bind every design: (1) a request carries **only the data the current step actually needs**, and (2) every computation that does **not** require server-side authority happens on the **client** — the **browser** for web, the **app** for mobile/native — from data already in hand. Putting work on Weegloo that Weegloo need not do is a **defect to fix**, not a style preference."
      - "**Order of operations — the two halves never conflict.** Narrow the set **on the server** (scope → filter → order → paginate → project), transfer the **smallest result that answers the screen**, then derive everything else **on the client**. \"Compute on the client\" is **never** a licence to pull a whole collection and sort it out locally — that is the worst of both, and when the rows carry anything the caller should not see it is a data-exposure bug as well."
      - "**This binds the agent's own calls too**, not only the code you generate: every `mcp__weegloo__*` read is subject to the same minimum-data discipline."
      - "**Before adding a request, ask three questions:** is this data **already loaded** (client state / cache)? can **one** request answer instead of **N**? does it change often enough to **re-fetch at all**? The cheapest request is the one you do not make."

  - section: Fetch the minimum — mandatory on every read
    items:
      - "**`select` on every read** — name the paths you will actually render. Standing obligation: *Projection* in **`weegloo-global-rules`**; mechanics in **`weegloo-api-query-optimization`**."
      - "**Filter and scope SERVER-SIDE, on the indexed axes** — `sys.contentType.sys.id`, status, `createdBy`, tags, `sys.id[in]`. Fetching broadly and filtering in memory is acceptable **only** when the loaded array is already the whole, bounded, small dataset; over a paginated or unknown-size collection it is both wasteful and silently **wrong** (it searches only the rows you happen to hold)."
      - "**`limit` = what the view renders** (max **100**, default **15**). Fetch further pages **only when the user asks for more** (`links.next` — **`weegloo-list-pagination`**). Never pre-walk every page to paint one screen."
      - "**A count is `totalCount`, never a walk.** Every list response carries **`totalCount`** — read it from a `limit=1&select=sys.id` request. Paging through a collection to count it is forbidden."
      - "**One request instead of N.** Expand references with **`include=1`** rather than a by-id fetch per row; batch with **`sys.id[in]`**; replace a loop of GETs with one filtered list. Conversely, do **not** `include` or `select` what the screen does not render."
      - "**Images: ask for the size you display.** Append the style preset segment (**`/style1`**…**`/style10`**) to a Media file URL for thumbnails and avatars instead of shipping the original and shrinking it in CSS (**`weegloo-api-query-optimization`**)."
      - "**Public / high-traffic reads go through CDA (or ACDA), not CMA/ACMA.** CDA is the **cache-based** delivery plane; routing browser or app read traffic through the management API bypasses that cache and loads the management plane for nothing."
      - "**Do not re-fetch what has not changed.** Hold results in client state across renders, mounts and route changes, and re-fetch on a **real signal** — a user action, a write you just made, an event — never on a timer."

  - section: Compute on the CLIENT — the default placement of work
    items:
      - "**The client does the arithmetic and the presentation.** All of this is client work, always, and is **never** a reason for another Weegloo request or a Script run: totals, subtotals, averages, percentages, min/max and other aggregates **over rows already loaded**; grouping, pivoting and chart series; sorting and filtering **within a loaded, complete set**; date/time math and timezone conversion; formatting, currency, number and i18n display; truncation, highlighting, derived labels and flags; form validation feedback; virtualization and paging of an already-loaded list."
      - "**Do not create Weegloo resources to hold what the client can derive.** A `summary` / `stats` / `total` Content rewritten on every change is a second source of truth **and** extra write load — compute it at render time from the rows, unless the value must be **authoritative** (next section)."
      - "**A Script must earn its run.** Script executions are a **monthly, Organization-wide allowance** shared by `/execute`, Webhook-run Scripts and Schedulers (**`weegloo-script`**, **`weegloo-scheduler`**) — a Script that only rearranges data the caller already holds spends that budget for nothing, and once the allowance is exhausted **every** Script and Scheduler in the Organization stops. Ask **\"does this need the server's authority?\"** — if the answer is no, it is client code."
      - "**Schedulers run at the slowest cadence that satisfies the requirement.** Each firing spends one execution and competes with the product's own traffic."

  - section: What must NOT move to the client (the counterweight)
    items:
      - "**Moving any of the following to the client is a security bug, not a saving** — each stays on Weegloo (a Script, a role, or a server-side query) whatever it costs:"
      - "  - anything that needs a **secret** — a third-party API key, an SMTP credential, a PG secret key (**`weegloo-script`** → *Secrets & auth*);"
      - "  - **authorization and trust** decisions — permission checks, payment **amount verification**, signature / webhook verification, credit or quota enforcement. A client-computed value is an **input to be verified**, never the truth;"
      - "  - **atomic multi-step writes** with compensation, and **concurrency-safe** updates of a shared row (`sys.version` optimistic locking);"
      - "  - **privilege delegation** — letting a low-privilege caller perform exactly one privileged operation;"
      - "  - any **query over a dataset the client does not (and must not) hold** — filtering, searching or counting there stays a server-side query with proper filters, and `fields.*` text search carries **`X-Weegloo-Advanced-Search: true`**."
      - "**Never over-fetch in order to compute locally.** If the client-side math would require pulling rows the caller should not see, or an unbounded set, that computation belongs **server-side by definition** — the minimum-data rule wins over the client-compute rule, never the other way round."

  - section: Forbidden load anti-patterns (fix on sight)
    items:
      - "**Polling loops.** No `setInterval` / retry loop re-fetching a list to notice a change — use a user action, a **Webhook** (event) or a **Scheduler** (clock). **One exception:** awaiting an async job you just created — poll **that single resource by `sys.id`**, projected, with **backoff**, a **bounded attempt count**, and a stop on the terminal state (**`weegloo-script`** → the external-API job pattern)."
      - "**Paging to count or to aggregate** — use `totalCount`, a server-side `ResourceCount`, or aggregate over a bounded loaded set."
      - "**N+1 by-id reads** to render a list — one filtered list (+ `include=1`) instead."
      - "**Fetch-all-then-filter** over a paginated or unknown-size collection."
      - "**Unprojected reads** — a `GetList*` / list GET with no `select` returns whole documents: every locale bucket of every field of every row."
      - "**A `fields.*` filter or `order` without `X-Weegloo-Advanced-Search: true`** — an unindexed scan that passes on seed data and times out as the Space fills up."
      - "**A request per keystroke** in a search box — debounce, require a minimum query length, and cancel the in-flight request."
      - "**Re-requesting on every render, mount or route change** instead of reusing client state."
